-- emit/app: a function referenced ONLY as an evidence argument survives
-- (`docs/design/backend.md` §9's third edge leg;
-- `static-dispatch-spike.md` §1.4, §8.2).
--
-- `eq` is the `eq` OF `Tagged`: a `pub` value of the module that declares
-- the type, which is what makes it that type's method (§1.2).
-- **Nothing in this file calls it by name.** `anyEqual` is
-- `where a.eq : a, a -> Bool`, so the call in `main` passes `eq` as a
-- hidden leading argument — a reference that no source line spells and that
-- `Bir.refs` therefore does not record.
--
-- The golden is that `DceEvidenceOnly$eq` is still emitted, that
-- `DceEvidenceOnly$anyEqual` is called with it in front of its own
-- arguments (§8.1), and that `byLength` came along with it on an ordinary
-- edge out of a declaration that only the evidence edge kept alive. Without
-- §9's dispatch-site leg the only edge out of `main` would be `anyEqual`,
-- both would be deleted, and the emitted call would name a `const` that is
-- not there — `ReferenceError` at load, after a build that exited 0.
-- `run/DceEvidenceDepth` is the same edge two levels deeper, where the
-- failure is observable by running.
--
-- `unusedMethod` is the control: a `pub` value of the same module, reaching
-- the same `byLength`, that no evidence position ever answers. It is gone,
-- and `byLength` is not.
import Node exposing (Program)
import String


pub type Tagged
    = Tagged String


pub eq : Tagged, Tagged -> Bool
eq a b = byLength a == byLength b


pub byLength : Tagged -> Int
byLength t =
    case t of
        Tagged text ->
            String.length text


pub unusedMethod : Tagged -> Int
unusedMethod t = byLength t + 1


pub anyEqual : a, a -> Bool
    where a.eq : a, a -> Bool
anyEqual x y = x.eq y


main : Program
main = Node.printLines [ String.fromInt (if anyEqual (Tagged "a") (Tagged "b") then 1 else 0) ]
